data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The user wants me to generate a title for a conversation. The message is a directive about reading campaign context files and following instructions from a specific input file (d002.md), then replying via a command.\n\nKey elements:\n- Campaign context from member.json\n- Input files listed\n- Specific task: d002.md\n- Dispatch ID: d002\n- Need to reply with summary\n\nTitle should focus on main topic/question. This is about executing campaign task d002. I should keep \"d002\" exact. The title should be ≤50 characters and a single line.\n\nPossible titles:\n- \"Campaign task d002 execution\"\n- \"Execute d002 campaign dispatch\"\n- \"d002 campaign input task\"\n- \"Process d002 campaign instruction\"\n- \"Campaign dispatch d002 follow-up\"\n\nLet me check character counts:\n- \"Campaign task d002 execution\" = 28 chars\n- \"Execute d002 campaign dispatch\" = 30 chars\n- \"d002 campaign input task\" = 24 chars\n- \"Process d002 campaign instruction\" = 33 chars\n- \"Campaign dispatch d002 follow-up\" = 32 chars\n\nAll are under 50. The message is about reading context and following d002.md, then replying. The main topic is the campaign task/dispatch d002.\n\nI think \"Campaign task d002 execution\" is clear and natural. Or \"Execute campaign dispatch d002\". Let me go with \"Execute campaign dispatch d002\" - 29 chars.\n\nWait, the rules say \"When a file is mentioned, focus on WHAT the user wants to do WITH the file, not just that they shared it.\" Here files are mentioned as context/instructions. The user wants to read them and follow d002.md. So focusing on executing the d002 dispatch makes sense.\n\nI'll output: Execute campaign dispatch d002"},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959430,"id":"chatcmpl-27534b7bfa974e2980372178ada0de33","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

